# Trivy vulnerability ignore list for rocOpt container images
#
# See VULNERABILITY_MITIGATIONS.md for full justification and review record.
# Do not add an entry here without a matching section in that file.
#
# Format: <CVE/GHSA-ID>  exp:<YYYY-MM-DD>  # one-line reason
# The exp: date forces Trivy to stop suppressing the finding and fail the
# scan again at the next review date, so stale ignores can't go unnoticed.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-10-05
# Source scan:   trivy-reports (4).zip, rocopt-1.0.0.amd0_rocm7.2.3.ubuntu24.04_py3.13, 2026-10-01
#
# Root cause: all four findings come from a dormant, unused `ensurepip`
# bootstrap wheel bundled by stock CPython 3.13, which carries pip's own
# vendored copies of msgpack/urllib3 and a text-only setuptools version
# reference. Already fixed in source (commits a6b0d032, 0b4268d1, e2fba1f6
# on amd-integration) by stripping that wheel from the image. These entries
# are suppressed only until a freshly rebuilt image confirms the findings
# are gone -- then delete these lines rather than renewing the exp: date.

# msgpack - pip's vendored copy inside the dormant ensurepip wheel; real
# top-level msgpack installed is 1.2.1 (fixed). Fix already merged.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2026-10-15 # msgpack: pip-vendored copy in dormant ensurepip wheel, fix merged e2fba1f6

# setuptools - version string referenced inside the same dormant wheel;
# real top-level setuptools installed is 80.10.2 (fixed). Fix already merged.
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2026-10-15 # setuptools: referenced in dormant ensurepip wheel, fix merged e2fba1f6

# urllib3 - pip's vendored copy inside the same dormant wheel; real
# top-level urllib3 installed is 2.8.0 (fixed). Same fix should cover this,
# unverified until next rebuild/rescan (advisories published 2026-09-29).
CVE-2026-97687 exp:2026-10-15 # urllib3: pip-vendored copy in dormant ensurepip wheel, same fix should apply
CVE-2026-97689 exp:2026-10-15 # urllib3: pip-vendored copy in dormant ensurepip wheel, same fix should apply
